<div class="c"><h1 class="redstar">Poetry By:Destiny</h1></div><h2 class="c">For The Moment</h2><p>I need you now<br>I make no assurances that it will always be thus<br>But rest assured<br>I need you now<br>And hope to need you throughout my life<br><br>I love you now<br>I make no promises for a lifetime<br>But rest assured<br>I love you now<br>But I hope to love you throughout my life<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Will Anything Last?</h2><p>What is there left, <br> That has not become tainted with filth?<br>Is there even anything left, <br> That has been left sacred and true?<br><br>Do not speak to me of love, <br> We all know the horror love brings.<br>Do not speak to me of peace, <br> We all know there is no such thing.<br><br>Speak to me not of friendship,<br> Because friends don't always last.<br>Speak to me not of living in the moment,<br> The time you realize it's there, it has passed.<br><br>Is there anything left, <br> That has not become tainted with unpleasentries?<br>Is there anything left<br> That will last through all our eternities.<br><br>Everything will pass, <br> And vanish through the fingertips of our time. <br>But it seems like the hardest thing to do sometimes, <br> Is remembering how to survive. <br><br>Our lives are not as infulential, <br> As we would love and try to believe, <br>The world has existed without us, <br> And will turn that cheek once more when we leave.<br><br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">8:12</h2><p>It's 5:12AM your time <br>And you are still in your dreams<br>The sun is a simple memory <br>On the other side of eternity is seems<br><br>It's 5:12AM your time <br>And I've already put part of my day aside<br>I've opened up another can of &quote;keep alive for the day&quote;<br>And I'm partly on my way <br><br>It's 5:12AM your time <br>And you don't know I'm here thinking of you <br>I've been writing to you all morning <br>But have nothing yet to send<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Not Hiding</h2><p>I sit in my little glass house<br>Watching you as you shout your obscenities at me <br>I sit in my little glass house<br>With only gravel and rocks everywhere I see<br><br>I made my little glass house<br>With the fire of passion we used to displace<br>I made my little glass house<br>Out of all that sand you ruthlessly kicked in my face<br><br>And I'm naked before you<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">I am Not a Poet</h2><p>I am not a poet<br>I'm a child writing down my feelings<br>Vaguely and unclearly<br><br>I am not an artist<br>I'm a child playing in finger paints and charcoal<br>Imitating and replicating the world as I see it<br><br>I am not a musician<br>I'm a child fumbling over strings and chords<br>Randomly shouting lyrics to the wind<br><br>I am neither poet, nor artist, nor musician<br>Because I do nothing but repeat the things I see or hear<br>Never creating<br>Like a child repeating things as it begins to grow up<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Again</h2><p>Hurt me again<br>It's nothing new <br>It's nothing painful anymore <br>Your stabbing has become only a growing pain <br>I always have survived <br><br>Blame me again<br>It's nothing new <br>It's nothing meaningful anymore<br>Your judgement is nothing but a self-defense<br>I always have survived <br><br>Hate me again <br>It's nothing new<br>It's nothing foreign anymore<br>Your loathing has never broken me in two<br>I always have survived <br><br>Burn me again <br>It~Rs nothing new<br>It's nothing blistering anymore<br>Your scars have done nothing but discolor my skin <br>I always have survived<br><br>Doubt me again <br>It's nothing new<br>It's nothing degrading anymore<br>Your disbelief has never made me doubt my own words<br>I always have survived<br><br>Brave me again<br>It's nothing new <br>It's nothing courageous anymore<br>Your steps have always lead back to me <br>I always have survived<br><br>Love me again<br>It's nothing new<br>It's nothing too honest anymore<br>You have always come back for more<br>Because I have always survived<br>I will never be overcome with malice<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Untitled</h2><p>By promising you nothing <br>I promise you everything<br>And tell no lies<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">As You Fall</h2><p><br>I will listen to you crackle as you fall <br>As everyone else ignores your tranquility <br>I will thrash in the calmness and fight the silence<br>Like a child in the midst of play<br><br>I will gaze at your beauty as you fall <br>As everyone cringes and shivers at your appearance<br>I will undress and suffer your cold fingertips<br>Like a lonely lover looking for solace<br><br>I will see you vanish as you fall <br>As everyone runs inside to watch you die<br>I will sit on my car hood and laugh at your coming<br>Like a smoker in the rain<br><br>I will watch you die as you hit the ground<br>As everyone else brushes you away <br>I will walk right through your remains and think of your life<br>Like a bug on my windshield<br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">English Winter</h2><p>I love the haze<br>I thrive on pretending I'm enduring an English winter<br>I like the thick mist <br>And I push my foot to the floor the thicker it gets<br>Tempting my fate, daring God to take action.<br><br>I love the haze<br>And the fantasy of an English winter<br>I like the thick mist <br>And how daring it all makes me feel <br>Alive in my numbness<br>As I push it harder and harder to the edge of the road<br><br>I love the haze<br>And I've grown accustomed to living in such a way<br>I cannot see in front <br>I cannot see behind<br>I can only see what I am in now <br>And it will never be any different<br><br>I love this English winter<br>Far away from all my torment <br>Far away from the place my pain thrives <br>Far away from all the people who demand so much from my life<br>Far away from the same old lies<br>And out of reach of all those terrible eyes that damn me for trying<br>And damn me if I don't<br><br>I sing and scream till I can scream no more <br>Or cough and choke through the force<br>And I plunge through the mist carelessly<br>Only seeing a foot or two ahead<br><br>I will curse it all before I am through <br>And I will leave it all behind<br>I will curse you all before I am through <br>And I will leave you all behind<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Tonight</h2><p>My father died tonight<br>And with him he took it all <br>Our peace of mind, <br> Our hope for reconciliation,<br>  Our prayers that the right thing will always prevail.<br><br>My father died tonight<br>And with him he took all of our burden<br>Our sorrow from the silence<br> Our pain from the attempts<br>  Our frustration at one man's hopelessness.<br><br>My father died tonight<br>And in his death he gave us everything.<br>An end pain we watched him suffer in <br> An end to the angst he brought upon himself<br>  A release from his tortured soul<br><br><br><br><br><br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">Leech</h2><p>You feed off the weaknesses I give you in trust<br>You feed off the weaknesses I give you in trust</p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"><h2 class="c">If You Leave</h2><p>I could crush myself <br>Under the weight of my own self analysis <br>But I have done that before <br>And I find the broken bones irritating reminders of my weakness<br><br>I could scream <br>For my torments that seemingly leave me voiceless<br>But I have done that before <br>And I despise my inability to speak clearly<br><br>I could cry <br>And purge myself of these tears I~Rm not sure should be released<br>But I have done that before <br>And it does nothing but swell my eyes as a vulgar reminder<br><br>I could become enraged at your youth<br>Make you hate me for something you think you have to do<br>But I have been in those shoes before<br>And my desire to know the emptiness of shallow love would have stopped at nothing <br><br>I could curse you for these things <br>That I myself have done <br>But I have done that before <br>And understand the need you think you feel<br><br>I could fight you <br>Make you stay here despite your doubts<br>But I have done that before <br>And have learned the offensiveness of such love<br>And wish to not be in that purgatory again<br></p><hr width="50%" class="redstar"></body>
